// PACT open type for Row 1 (ANNOTATIONS.md) — adbg_axi_biu.sv.
// Full cycle-by-cycle protocol prose (both boundaries): see PROTOCOL.md in this
// directory. This file only encodes the AXI-facing S_AXIADDR/S_AXIDATA behavior
// documented there (the debug-host pool below encodes PROTOCOL.md's other half).
//
// PROTOCOL.md's key finding for the bug: in S_AXIADDR the manager asserts aw_valid
// AND w_valid EVERY cycle it remains in that state (recomputed combinationally,
// not latched), so aw_req/w_req below are levels the manager keeps re-driving
// until each is independently granted — NOT a single-shot pair of actions. Three
// exits exist from S_AXIADDR (lines 535-540):
//   - aw_ready&&!w_ready this cycle -> S_AXIDATA (w_req kept re-driven alone there
//     until w_gnt; aw_req now stays low, so AW can never be re-offered again).
//   - aw_ready&&w_ready this cycle  -> S_AXIRESP directly (both close together).
//   - !aw_ready (regardless of w_ready, INCLUDING w_ready=1) -> next_fsm_state
//     keeps its default = current state, i.e. stay in S_AXIADDR and re-assert
//     aw_req/w_req identically next cycle. If the subordinate granted w_gnt on
//     this stalled cycle (legal — AMBA lets W close before AW), the manager has
//     no state that remembers that: it goes on offering w_req again next cycle
//     with no path to AXIRESP until aw_gnt is *also* seen. `biu_axi_itfc`'s `X`
//     branch below is exactly this: w_req may repeat one or more times while
//     aw_req is still outstanding, and only ends when aw_gnt finally arrives.
//
// `legal_subordinate_itfc` types a spec-legal AXI subordinate that may grant
// w_gnt before aw_gnt (AMBA does not require AW-before-W acceptance, and does
// not require the manager to keep re-offering a beat that already closed).
// Composed: the subordinate's w-first branch grants w_gnt while aw_req is still
// pending: the manager's type has no way to record that and continues re-driving
// w_req, which the subordinate's type (a single w! per transaction) has already
// moved past — Row 1 is closed-pairwise: no environment reconciles a subordinate
// that may answer w-first with a manager whose only forward-progress edge needs
// aw_gnt specifically, regardless of w_gnt's own state.

pool adbg_axi_biu_pool {
    ep_le -- ep_ri : ch;
    i1 : rec X . ^(
        ep.aw_req : rec Y . ^(ep.w_req, * : #1;Y),
        * : #1;X
    );#1,
    i2 : ep.w_req;#1;ep.aw_req;#1
}